  "result": "`satisfies(version, range)` is implemented in `src/semver.js` and `npm test` passes: 113 tests, 0 failed. The new tests are in `test/satisfies.test.js` and cover every table in `docs/SPEC.md`, plus invalid inputs and prerelease edge cases. The suite passes only after I corrected two test cases of my own that had wrong expectations.\n\nFor cases the spec doesn't cover, I made these choices:\n- **Wildcards:** a wildcard in one position makes every later position a wildcard too, so `1.x.3` is treated as `1.x`.\n- **`>*` and `<*`:** these match nothing.\n- **Operators on `~` and `^`:** whitespace after them is allowed, e.g. `~ 1.2.3`.\n- **Prerelease identifiers:** numeric ones with leading zeros are accepted. The spec only bans leading zeros in major/minor/patch.\n- **Very large numbers:** these compare exactly, since versions are kept as digit strings rather than JS numbers.",
